## Overview

This adds an opt-in specialized decode path for GLM-5.3 (`GlmMoeDsaForCausalLM`) for single-request serving on 8xB200 (SM100) and 8xB300 (SM103) at TP8. Turn it on with `--additional-config '{"decode_backend": "latency_specialized"}'`.

With the switch on, CuTe DSL kernels replace vLLM's FULL uniform-decode CUDA graph for the 78 target layers:
- a sharded sparse-attention selector;
- a fused MLA worker;
- a fused MoE that reads vLLM's DeepGEMM expert layout in place;
- the dense FFN;
- the LM head.

